│ patch_name               │ shared_evenodd_rots_reduce_params                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce ansatz parameter count per block by reusing rotation parameters across qubits with │
│                          │ even/odd wire parity (parameter sharing via identical `param` strings). Concretely:       │
│                          │ - Replace per-qubit RY with two shared parameters: `ry_e` (even wires) and `ry_o` (odd    │
│                          │ wires).                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Replace per-qubit RZ layers (pre and post) with two shared parameters each:             │
│                          │ `rz_pre_e/rz_pre_o` and `rz_post_e/rz_post_o`.                                            │
│                          │ - Keep the fixed CZ entangling chain unchanged.                                           │
│                          │ This dramatically lowers `n_params` (thus optimizer work and overfitting risk) while      │
│                          │ preserving enough variational freedom for the 3× reuploading and 2× block repetition to   │
│                          │ learn decision boundaries.                                                                │
