│                          │ parameterized RX and RY rotations on all qubits to maximize feature representation        │
│                          │ capacity. This is followed by a "staircase" chain of CRZ gates (0-1, 1-2, ..., 7-0) which │
│                          │ facilitates non-local correlation buildup across the qubit register. A subsequent layer   │
│                          │ of fixed CZ gates ensures sufficient mixing to prevent the state from becoming too        │
│                          │ sparse. This structure is designed to better capture the correlations between binary      │
│                          │ features in the 8-qubit space, leading to more robust generalization.                     │
