│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Make the ansatz more parameter-efficient and better aligned with typical expressivity     │
│                          │ patterns for ZZ/phase feature maps:                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Replace the current RX+RY-per-qubit (16 params/block) with only RY (8 params/block).    │
│                          │ - Introduce only two *shared* global RZ calibration parameters per block (applied to all  │
│                          │ qubits), instead of many independent RZ/phase degrees of freedom.                         │
│                          │ - Keep a CZ “ring backbone” (fixed, no parameters).                                       │
│                          │ - Add only two parametrized CRZ “odd/even” layers, where each layer reuses the same       │
│                          │ parameter across 4 edges (2 params/block).                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should reduce total circuit parameters substantially (better parameter efficiency)   │
│                          │ while retaining enough tunable controlled-phase structure to fit the data, improving      │
│                          │ convergence speed/validation/generalization.                                              │
