                         Patch Metadata - Gen 14/20 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_rz_czring_sparsecrz_reuploadfriendly                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current ansatz block (which uses independent RX and RY on every qubit,        │
│                          │ creating 16 single-qubit parameters plus 8 CRZ parameters per block) with a more          │
│                          │ parameter-efficient but still expressive structure:                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Use only one trainable single-qubit rotation type per qubit (RY) to reduce redundant    │
│                          │ degrees of freedom while retaining universality with re-uploading.                        │
│                          │ - Add shared (parameter-reused) global RZ layers to capture per-qubit phase offsets       │
│                          │ without increasing the parameter count linearly with qubits.                              │
│                          │ - Keep a CZ “ring backbone” plus an additional fixed CZ layer to ensure strong            │
│                          │ connectivity/correlation capacity at low parameter cost.                                  │
│                          │ - Use sparse, disjoint CRZ controlled-phase parameters to add nontrivial entangling       │
│                          │ expressivity, but with far fewer parameters than the current dense staircase.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targets higher combined score primarily via improved parameter efficiency (lower     │
│                          │ n_params) while maintaining (or improving) validation/test accuracy and keeping           │
│                          │ generalization gap low.                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0030                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-nano                                                            │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'low'}                                                                         │
