│ patch_description        │ Make the final phase-rotation layer parameter-efficient by replacing the two              │
│                          │ symmetry-shared RZ keys (“rz_final_even” on {0,2,4,6} and “rz_final_odd” on {1,3,5,7})    │
│                          │ with a single shared key applied to all 8 qubits.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the number of trainable circuit parameters per ansatz block (from 14 → 13),  │
│                          │ improving parameter efficiency while keeping the overall circuit structure (same          │
│                          │ uploads/repeats, same entanglers, same mixing RY layer) and the expressivity largely      │
│                          │ intact. Since the previous variants already achieved perfect accuracy, this targets the   │
│                          │ remaining objective: lower loss and faster convergence with fewer parameters.             │
